Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Remote Preflight Private Permit Bridge P0 Requirements Analysis

@ [analysis_uuid] 5a54adce-4cc5-45cf-b723-fc73709e7a66
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] 750fbbb5-f72f-4816-882f-d8b0ebf1acc7

& [RequiredMeaning]
  + one future opaque live admission must carry exact activation decision proposal producer-plan and publication correspondence without being cloneable serializable persistent or publicly constructible
  + one crate-private bridge must prevalidate every provider-free input before consuming the admission to ask the runner module for exactly one permit
  + one crate-private runner issuer must consume the admission by value construct the existing exact-scope permit and return it only to the bridge
  + the bridge must immediately move the permit into exactly one existing runner entry and cannot loop retry return replace persist or recover either capability
  + every result after permit issuance is terminal; a runner fault is abandoned_after_consumption and a successful run is not accepted until canonical reparse and existing receipt validation both pass

& [RequiredProof]
  + exact visibility module ownership type traits field privacy lineage cardinality sequencing failure and terminal invariants
  + static absence gates for public export CLI ambient trigger alternate process path constructors serialization cloning persistence loops retries and live-initiation code
  + provider-free unit fixtures exercise pre-mint refusal one-shot callback consumption post-consumption failure provider-unavailable projection receipt tamper and terminal no-reentry
  + formation verification passes PowerShell7 and WindowsPowerShell5.1 with every live counter zero

& [Deferred]
  + production admission construction operator identity signing-key custody trusted time consent revocation replay ledger physical invocation and terminal evidence publication remain a separately source-governed live-initiation phase
